This will close ALL open submenus of the root menu. In our case, the root menu is the menubar. The About submenu is open (so it is a child of the root menu). Therefore, closeChildren() on the root menu will close the About submenu as well.

We only want to close the current submenu (the Facts submenu) and then move focus to the parent menu item (which is the Facts item) in the parent menu (the About menu).

Instead, we should:

  1. Close the current submenu (the Facts submenu) -> which is controlled by the toggle of the Facts item.
  2. Then move focus to the Facts item (which is in the About menu).

But note: the Facts item is in the About menu. The About menu is a submenu of the root menubar.

